WEBVTT

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.540
Ikuto the Digimon Kid

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.540
The Forest's Keeper, Jureimon

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.950
Ikuto the Digimon Kid!

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.540
The Forest's Keeper, Jureimon!

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.680
Masaru and the others found themselves completely outmatched by the sudden appearance of Mercurimon.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.950
However, Masaru's desire to protect everyone called forth a new Digisoul,

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:31.320
and GeoGreymon evolved to his Perfect form, RiseGreymon.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.110
Furthermore, our heroes suspected that all of the Digimon cases

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:45.010
that had occurred in the human world may have been instigated by Mercurimon.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:48.440
To stop him, they decided to head for the Digital World.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.520
Wait.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.830
There's something I must tell all of you.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.650
Especially you, Masaru.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.310
This is important information concerning your father.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.770
My... Dad?

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:05.840
Yes.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.440
It occurred ten years ago,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.520
when we discovered a world that existed in a different dimension from our world - the Digital World.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.350
The National Government's Ministry of Confidentiality gathered people who specialized in various fields,

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.850
and sent us to investigate the Digital World.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.790
Our group met with severe difficulties.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:29.130
We were attacked by Digimon, our camp was destroyed,

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:34.300
and we were in danger of being unable to return back to the human world.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.750
But under one man's capable orders...

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.000
the exploration squad avoided disaster,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.100
and we were able to safely return home.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.810
That man was Professor Daimon Suguru.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.140
Your father.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:03.410
Professor Daimon's whereabouts in the Digital World became unknown after that.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.110
Even today, we have no idea where he may be.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.000
Mom...

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.000
Mom, did you know about this?!

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.130
Yes.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.050
It's true that Suguru-san was the leading man in Digimon research.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.520
He was always looking for a way that would allow the humans and Digimon to live together in peace.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.900
So you knew.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.980
You knew everything.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.440
That's why you weren't surprised when you saw me.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.160
I was never planning on hiding it.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:48.500
But I thought if you knew the truth, Masaru, you would also disappear to the Digital World...

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.660
I'm not going anywhere!

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.840
I'm sure Dad will come back someday, too! Got it?

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:56.570
Masaru...

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.660
Don't you worry about anything!

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.310
Leave everything to me!

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.110
Aniki...

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:05.740
I'll go to the Digital World, defeat Mercurimon,

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.470
and find Dad for sure!

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.940
You really are his son.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.440
M-Mom?

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.760
Promise me...

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.400
that you'll definitely come back.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:25.370
I don't want both my beloved husband and my son to be stolen from me by the Digital World.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:26.830
Gotcha.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.830
I'll never do anything that'll make you sad.{onkei: Masaru forgot his promise...... orz} {Splash: D: waaaaaa}

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.790
Masaru...

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.250
TOP SECRET

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.250
Unable to access

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.250
Please re-enter the password

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.250
No good.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.720
All data concerning Professor Daimon is confidential.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.750
Even so...

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.680
Who would have guessed that Masaru's father was the leading man in Digimon research...

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.140
I wonder what happened to him?

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.720
This smells dangerous.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.270
Still...

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.690
It's worth checking out.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.790
The Digital World is still an unknown world enveloped in mystery.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:16.580
There will undoubtedly be threats awaiting there that we have no way of expecting.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:17.910
In the worst-case scenario...

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:21.550
you may not be able to come back to the human world just like Professor Daimon.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.650
Are you still determined to go?

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.010
Hello? Mom?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.010
No, there's no reason I called...

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.600
If there is no change in your minds,

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:34.200
Yeah.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.820
then gather here tomorrow morning at 0830.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.230
It's huge!

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.140
Mom made these lunches for all of us.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.490
That's too much...

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.670
We're not going on a picnic...

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.500
Aniki...

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.090
Tohma says he doesn't want Sayuri's fried eggs.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.170
No choice then.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.210
We'll just have to eat it all ourselves.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.670
Master is afflicted...

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.300
You must really love those fried eggs...

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.150
Wow...

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.180
So you've all decided.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:14.550
This is a Digimon radar, which will be sent along with everything else in one container.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:17.410
It'll tell you the general area where Mercurimon is.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.830
This is a long-range communicator.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.400
Use it to give us regular updates.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.190
What are these?

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.860
They're transmission markers.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:30.730
The signal they emit will let us know where to open the Digital Gate for you.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.330
Don't lose them, or we won't be able to bring you back.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.050
So they're like tracking devices.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.290
What about the transporting equipment?

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:42.390
After consulting all of the data on our last Dive, I made some adjustments.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:43.500
It's perfectly safe.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.010
All your preparations are complete.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:47.250
Now then...

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.180
Begin the mission!

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.280
Roger!

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.280
Roger!

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.560
Transportation bumper accumulating at 98%.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.060
Bionic Condenser functioning!

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.770
Digital Harmonizer aligning.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.860
Security opening.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:03.860
Stabilizer tuning up.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.130
Digital Gate Open!

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.440
Countdown!

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.390
3...

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:09.390
2...

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.460
1...

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.410
Begin transportation!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.910
Beginning transportation!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.910
Beginning transportation!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.370
Was it really a good idea Satsuma

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.280
to let them go?

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.100
I want to believe in those children,

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.640
and the unlimited potential they hold.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.260
They're here.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.010
Transportation complete.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.090
So this is the Digital World...

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:01.690
There are rocks and things floating in the sky...

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.210
It's unbelievable...

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.090
Hehe, surprised, aren't you?

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.010
Why are you acting so smug?

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.190
Because this is my second time here.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:10.530
I'm already an expert.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:11.690
Oh, really?

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.890
There's the container.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:13.720
Let's go!

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:17.070
Why couldn't they send it a little closer to us?

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.650
Just wait here then.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:20.730
We'll eat the lunches in the meantime.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:21.240
Huh?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:21.970
Aniki!

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:22.850
Agumon...

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:25.700
That container has Sayuri's lunches too!

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.470
That's why Tohma's in such a rush!

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.590
Wait up!

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:34.230
Hey, you don't think Mercurimon will show up right now, do you?

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:42.410
Hey, Agumon!

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.990
What are you doing outside?!

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.560
I'll be the first to get Sayuri's fried eggs!

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.970
Sayuri's fried eggs...!

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.090
Gaomon, Realize!

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.610
Lalamon, Realize!

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:08.800
Yes, Master!

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.350
La~la~mon!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.910
We've lost Masaru and the others!

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.290
The signal indicator to the porthole has also died out!

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:24.810
What?!

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:26.840
Satsuma...

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:34.950
Masaru!

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:35.860
Where are you going?

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.820
Duh, I'm going after him!

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:38.990
C'mon, Agumon!

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:39.780
Okay!

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.110
Stop!

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:42.110
It's dangerous!

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.490
Wait up!

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.110
Hold it right there!

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:52.770
Who is that kid?

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.460
Is he a... human boy?

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:55.770
That can't be possible!

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:06.490
Hey, you, hold it!

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:07.890
Yoshino!

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:09.100
Yoshino!

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.790
Ikuto!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.880
Falcomon!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.200
I was looking all over for you!

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.490
Where'd you go?

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:25.910
NOTE: Ikuto speaks in broken Japanese.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:20.990
Humans here.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:23.450
Those guys came here?

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:25.910
I never forgive humans!

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:26.810
Ikuto!

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.500
Gotcha, you shitty little punk!

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.290
Let go of Ikuto!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.620
Damn it...

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:44.140
Are you running away?!

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:50.520
You're...!

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.520
<i>Who the hell are you?!</i>

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:54.270
<i>Give back the egg!</i>

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.690
He's that Falcomon guy!

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:59.400
Then does that mean that kid's with Mercurimon?

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:01.840
You guys enemy of Digimon!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.370
I defeat you!

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:04.530
What?!

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.570
Humans destroy Digital World's peace!

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:09.490
I not forgive humans!

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.700
Don't be stupid!

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:13.600
It's Mercurimon who destroyed the peace!

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.760
Don't talk bad of Mercurimon!

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.410
Mercurimon right!

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.050
All Digimon obey him!

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.730
Uchitake Otoshi!

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.730
Uchitake Drop

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.780
This is the worst...

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:52.580
Get... out...

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:56.170
What's with this fog?

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:03.810
Get out... of my forest!

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:05.640
Who's that?

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.520
What are these things?!

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:18.050
Lalamon!

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:18.920
Gaomon!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.120
Lala Screw!

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.400
Double Backhand!

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.260
Are you okay?

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.450
Damn it, what's going on?

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:34.410
You foolish and violent humans...

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:39.880
Leave this forest at once!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:48.850
Jureimon

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:48.850
Perfect Level

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:41.910
Jureimon.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:45.090
A Perfect Level Digimon that sends out a mist showing illusions.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:48.850
He grabs opponents with his ivy and eats them for his own nourishment.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:52.600
Is he also one of Mercurimon's pals?

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:56.020
I am the master of this forest.

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.040
I make no outside alliances.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:58.520
What?

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:02.730
The two young chicks who are hiding over there...

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.190
This goes for you as well.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:09.200
Leave this forest at once!

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.320
He's not on either side?

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:16.160
This must mean not all of the Digimon in the Digital World obey Mercurimon.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:18.170
Shut up!

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.340
Humans enemy of Digimon!

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:21.630
I will defeat humans!

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:24.090
Are you still blabbing about that?

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:27.210
Ikuto, give me power!

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:28.010
Okay!

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:31.790
That's...!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.470
A Digivice!

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:33.890
What's going on?

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:39.530
Falcomon, evolve!

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:57.850
Peckmon!

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:08.340
Peckmon

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:08.340
Adult Level

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:00.250
Peckmon.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.980
An Adult Level Digimon with indefatigable walking power.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.630
His special attack is Spiral Claw.

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:08.340
Spinning his entire body at high speed, he can pulverize the enemy with his enormous claws.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:12.610
Let's go, Peckmon!

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:17.500
Spiral Claw!

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:23.190
What incredible speed!

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:29.080
Digisoul Charge!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.750
Digisoul Charge!

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.990
Gaomon, evolve!

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.700
Gaogamon!

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:53.810
Lalamon, evolve!

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:05.900
Sunflowmon!

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:10.290
I fight!

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.180
I protect Digital World!

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.930
Since you don't know, I'll tell you!

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:28.680
You just picked a fight with Japan's number one street fighter!

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.950
Digisoul Charge!

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:41.330
Agumon, evolve!

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:57.970
GeoGreymon!

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:03.790
Horn Impulse!

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.020
Useless!

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.130
Kunai Bane!

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.130
Kunai Feathers

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.950
Stop!

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.640
Stop this!

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:18.180
Just when I came...

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:20.100
Just when I came to confirm my suspicions...

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.430
That bratty Ikuto!

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:22.850
What is he doing?!

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:29.820
Yanmamon

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:29.820
Adult Level

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:24.580
Yanmamon.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:27.580
An Adult Level Digimon whose body is covered in a hard shell.

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:29.820
He flies freely in the sky with the wings on his back!

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.070
Severely!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.020
I must punish him severely!

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:35.630
Dash Double Claw!

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:41.240
Sunshine Beam!

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:47.080
He's too fast!

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:49.430
Stop this!

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:51.360
Cherry Bomb!

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:58.220
Do you not understand what it means to stop?!

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:04.180
Those are...

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.560
Nyokimon

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.560
Baby Level

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:10.240
Nyokimon?

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.650
They're a Baby Level, Seed type Digimon.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:13.440
Oh...

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.030
Jureimon was protecting them...

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.480
Damn it!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:28.790
Everything...

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:31.000
Destroy everything!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.700
How can this be...

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.760
Spiral Blow!

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:45.060
Sunshine Beam!

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:48.440
What?

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.970
We all could use some help in our times of need.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.400
Go, GeoGreymon!

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:55.080
Mega Flame!

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.280
Spiral Blow!

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.280
Sunshine Beam!

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:05.930
Damn, it's too big!

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.000
Don't you give up!

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:11.280
Nothing's impossible for a man when he's put his entire soul into his fist!

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:15.390
Digisoul...

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.810
Full Charge!

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.880
GeoGreymon, evolve!

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:43.950
RiseGreymon!

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:50.740
Take it down, RiseGreymon!

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:51.540
Got it!

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.990
Trident Revolver!

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:08.320
What power...

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.170
Doesn't matter!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:10.370
I fight!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:10.890
But look!

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:15.860
If we fight any more, we'll drag them into this!

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.230
Let's retreat for now.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.060
Guess it's all over.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.860
That was a cinch, Aniki!

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:28.990
Unbelievable...

00:19:28.990 --> 00:19:34.040
We were saved by the foolish and vicious humans...

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:35.830
Don't worry about it.

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:40.150
It's true that a lot of humans are stupid, just like you say.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.430
But y'know...

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:43.440
Because they're stupid, they can get passionate about things.

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.500
They can even rush forward to save strange Digimon without a second thought.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:47.430
I see...

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:51.480
Even so, who was that Ikuto boy?

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:52.620
Who cares?!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:55.890
The next time he shows his face, I'm taking him down!

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:57.900
Never mind that, what are we going to do now?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:58.540
Huh?

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.360
All the equipment we brought is gone!

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:03.730
How are we going to find Mercurimon?

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:06.350
How are we going to get back home?!

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:11.190
As my thanks for helping the Nyokimon,

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.690
I will tell you one thing.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:18.300
In the palace where Mercurimon lives,

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:21.020
I've heard that there lies a Digital Gate.

00:20:21.020 --> 00:20:23.260
You know where Mercurimon is?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.220
Beyond that mountain.

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:30.200
In a place called Infinity Ice Ridge...

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.230
That is where Mercurimon's palace resides.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.150
Infinity Ice Ridge?

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:41.610
Whether or not you make it there is up to you.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.830
Nothing ventured, nothing gained.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:46.950
Things have become quite bothersome.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:48.120
Really?

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:53.420
From what I'm hearing, we can't go back to our world until we defeat Mercurimon.

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.300
How can it get any simpler than that?

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:56.580
You've got it right, Aniki!

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:57.530
All right then!

00:20:57.530 --> 00:20:59.700
Let's move out!

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.340
We... have to walk, do we?

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:03.290
This might make our calves fat!

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.590
This is the worst!

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:05.820
This is...

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.670
This is a wretched situation!

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:15.400
Mercurimon-sama!

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:16.980
Mercurimon-sama!

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:19.270
What...

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:22.390
What shall we do with those humans?!

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.080
Let them go.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:26.550
Oh dear.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:27.200
Oh dear!

